# Frontend configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local        # .env.local is git ignored
#
# Optional for a local run: the only value below already defaults to the port
# the Go API listens on, so `npm run dev` works with no file at all.
#
# Two things about Vite environment variables:
#
#  1. Only names beginning with VITE_ reach the browser — and everything that
#     does is compiled into the bundle, readable by anyone who opens the site.
#     So nothing secret may go in this file. The token signing secret is the
#     backend's JWT_SECRET and has no business anywhere near here.
#
#  2. The value is baked in when the app is built, not read when it starts.
#     Changing it means rebuilding; setting it in a deployed container's
#     environment does nothing.


# Base URL of the Go API: scheme, host and port, no path. A trailing slash is
# tolerated. It has to match where the backend actually listens (its
# HTTP_ADDRESS), and that backend has to list this app's own origin in its
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, or the browser refuses the response.
#
# Required for a production build, where the API is not on localhost.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4201


# The dev server's own port is not read from here: it is pinned to 4200 with
# `strictPort` in vite.config.ts, because the backend's CORS allowlist names
# that exact port and silently moving to another port would only produce a confusing
# browser error.
